REQUEST (maintainer)
Bare `karr` (and `karr board`) currently always renders every done task; on a
living board the Done section grows forever and drowns the actual open work.

SPEC
- Default `karr` / `karr board`: do NOT list tasks in status `done` (section
  omitted like the empty-archived case, Board.pm:144ff). Instead give a compact
  hint so the info is not silently lost, e.g. footer "5 tasks (4 done hidden)".
- New Board option `--done`: render the Done section as today.
- Must work identically for bare `karr --done` (routes via App::karr::execute
  -> Cmd::Board->new, App/karr.pm:230-237 — option needs plumbing) and
  `karr board --done`.
- Applies to all board output modes consistently (incl. --json/--tags if
  present); `karr list` is untouched (already excludes done by default).
- Empty done => no hint, output as today.

PARITY NOTE: deliberate deviation from kanban-md (Go board always shows done,
cmd/board.go only excludes archived). Maintainer decision on 2026-07-02.
Scope-Klarstellung: --compact bleibt unveraendert (eine Zeile pro Status mit Count+IDs, kein Wachstumsproblem — Counts dort gewollt). Hiding gilt fuer Default-Rendering, --tags und --json; --done schaltet ueberall frei. Soll gepinnt in t/37 (erweitert) + t/40 (neu, CLI-Plumbing bare karr --done via IPC::Open3).
Implemented and committed on main as 0eb982c: Done section hidden by default in karr/karr board (default, --tags, --json; JSON keeps done column+count, empties tasks), footer hint '(N done hidden)', new --done flag incl. bare-karr plumbing, --compact unchanged. Tests t/37 extended + t/40 new (CLI plumbing). Suite 38 files / 212 tests PASS. E2E verified on the real board.
